-- title:
--   Size of the comparison source for the metric class
-- statement:
--   Notation. $S=[-3,3]^2$ is the model square; a metric is a smooth positive matrix field $g$; $z$ is a scalar height; $H=\nabla_g^2z$ is its covariant Hessian; $K_g$ is the Gaussian curvature; $E=\det g\,(1-|dz|_g^2)$; $q=H_{xy}/H_{yy}$ is the Hessian quotient; $\kappa(x^2-h(y))$ is the model curvature; the patch box and the central box are the squares $[-1/10,1/10]^2$ and $[-1/5,1/5]^2$; the sheared coordinates are $\xi=x,\ \theta=y+q_0x$, with sheared height $z_s$; $L$ and $v_*$ are the class width and speed of (4.2); $\tilde g_\tau$ is the test metric (4.12) built from $g_*$; a bounded admissible height of bound $M$ is an admissible height with (4.1).
--
--   With $g_*$, $G,d,\kappa,q_0,r,M$ as above, $g_*$ of $C^2$ bound $G$ with $\det g_*\ge d$ on $S$, $N>2$ and $C_{\mathrm{res}}\ge0$, there is $C_{\mathrm{source}}>0$ such that for $0<\delta\le1/2$ and all large $\tau$ (with $\tau\ge1$): for every patch perturbation $\eta$, flow data and bounded admissible height $z$ of bound $M$ with the usual bounds, $g$ within $\tau^{-\tau}$ of the test metric, and every function $P$ with $|Q$-residual$_{g_*}(P)|\le C_{\mathrm{res}}\tau^{-N}$ on the strip of half-width $Lr/2$, the comparison source satisfies on that strip
--
--   $$|F(p)|\le C_{\mathrm{source}}\,\tau^{2-N}.$$
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This is the upstream Lean declaration `OAI.SmoothLocal.Perturbation.exists_actual_class_comparison_source_bound_at_radius` in `lean/OAI/Geometry/IsometricImmersion/Comparison/ActualClassComparisonSourceBound.lean`, stated verbatim; the Lean statement is authoritative for the precise hypotheses. It is an intermediate result of OpenAI's formalization.
